(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Functions, built-in functions, cells, code objects and modules."] [13 1 "// Function is a Python function: a code object with its globals, defaults and closure"] [14 1 "// (CPython's PyFunctionObject)."] [21 20 "// positional defaults, or nil"] [22 20 "// keyword-only defaults, or nil"] [24 20 "// __annotate__, or nil"] [25 20 "// __type_params__, or nil"] [26 20 "// __dict__, made on first use"] [29 2 "// GlobalsMap is the globals when FunctionType(code, globals) was given a dict subclass's instance (queue 205f:"] [30 2 "// annotationlib's _StringifierDict), Globals its dict: the function's global loads go through its __getitem__"] [31 2 "// (CPython's LOAD_GLOBAL on non-exact globals, PyMapping_GetOptionalItem: its __missing__), nil for a dict"] [37 1 "// Builtin is a function implemented in Go (CPython's builtin_function_or_method)."] [41 14 "// the bound object of a method, or nil"] [42 2 "// objectDescr: object's method that left object's dict through the class (methodDescrs[b] is ObjectType)"] [44 2 "// Owner is the type a method of a built-in type's dict belongs to (d_type, m_class's); unchecked: a class or"] [45 2 "// static method, its first argument no instance of Owner"] [48 2 "// wakeup: a task's task_wakeup, a node of finalize.go's graph (a pending task's cycle runs through it)"] [54 1 "// Cell is a closure's cell; Value nil is empty (unbound)."] [59 1 "// CodeObject is a code object as a Python value (the IR's {:code ...} constants)."] [64 1 "// Module is a module: its name and namespace."] [68 2 "// Cls is a subclass of module this module is an instance of (six's _LazyModule, queue 205), nil for module itself"] [70 2 "// slots are a subclass's __slots__' values (queue 226)"] [81 1 "// builtinFuncModules are the built-in modules' functions' modules (PY6d's REQUEST: a function's __module__,"] [82 1 "// CPython's m_module, which pickle saves it by)."] [99 4 "// method_vectorcall's check: a method descriptor called with its instance first"] [108 37 "// one allocation (queue 210: append grew it a second time)"] [113 4 "// method_check_args (PY7: dict.update() was a Go panic, test_ordered_dict's"] [114 4 "// CPythonBuiltinDictTests.test_update)"] [121 2 "// meth_richcompare: the same function of the same object; meth_hash not from the object's own hash"] [141 62 "// meth_repr"] [146 2 "// builtin_function_or_method's __module__ (PY6d's REQUEST): a module's function's module, a builtin's"] [147 2 "// \"builtins\", else None (pickle's whichmodule then finds the function in sys.modules)"] [163 2 "// methodobject.c's meth_reduce (PY6d's REQUEST: pickle saves a built-in function by name): a function's"] [164 2 "// qualified name, a bound method as getattr(self, name)"] [176 3 "// CPython's \"at 0x...\", the address an identity number (asyncio's Handle reprs and their tests: PY6h's"] [177 3 "// REQUEST, queue 200)"] [186 2 "// cell([contents]): Objects/cellobject.c's cell_new, cell_repr and cell_richcompare (queue 205f: annotationlib's"] [187 2 "// _build_closure makes the stringifiers' cells)"] [208 35 "// tp_richcompare without tp_hash: hash() refuses a cell"] [218 3 "// empty cells come before anything else (cell_compare_impl)"] [244 3 "// module_repr: importlib's _module_repr once importlib is the import system (PY6b's request)"] [250 4 "// importlib's _module_repr: a module with a location is \"from\" it"] [255 2 "// module(name, doc=None), CPython's module_init; a subclass's instance (queue 205: six's _MovedItems) made empty"] [256 2 "// as new_module makes it, its __init__ (module.__init__ through super()) filling it"] [279 2 "// module_new: an uninitialized module (its dict empty), any arguments; module_init fills it"] [295 2 "// module_getsets: __annotations__ and __annotate__ (PEP 649), data descriptors before the dict"] [300 38 "// a subclass's instance: its class's data descriptors first"] [328 4 "// a subclass's instance: the generic lookup (its class's descriptors around the dict), then the"] [329 4 "// dict's __getattr__ (module_getattro)"] [341 23 "// PY6a (enum's global_enum): module_getattro's data descriptors first"] [352 3 "// the type's methods (__dir__, __repr__ ...), then the module's __getattr__ (PEP 562)"] [361 2 "// module.__dir__ (module_dir, queue 223: traceback's suggestions call it): the dict's __dir__ function called,"] [362 2 "// else the dict's keys"] [382 1 "// functionNew is function(code, globals, name=None, argdefs=None, closure=None, kwdefaults=None), types.FunctionType"] [383 1 "// called: Objects/funcobject.c's func_new (its clinic's argument checks, then func_new_impl's in its order, and their"] [384 1 "// messages) over PyFunction_New (the code's name, qualname and docstring, the globals' __name__ as __module__, the"] [385 1 "// builtins from the globals' __builtins__). Queue 205f: annotationlib's FORWARDREF and STRING formats call an"] [386 1 "// __annotate__'s code with a _StringifierDict as its globals (typing.NamedTuple's annotated classes, pip's import)."] [452 2 "// _PyEval_BuiltinsFromGlobals: the globals' __builtins__ (a module its dict), else the running frame's"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[87 58] [88 39] [103 26] [115 27] [141 34] [150 31] [153 36] [157 58] [170 34] [189 38] [192 41] [245 42] [249 47] [287 28] [334 41] [349 39] [353 51] [356 40] [375 30] [400 12] [400 19] [409 31] [415 34] [421 34] [429 37] [442 29] [445 12] [445 19] [453 40] [454 26] [456 31] [461 26]]} (go/file "func.go" :imports [])

